From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 23:25:57 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] venus: give an oversized shmem allocation a shmem of its own

vn_renderer_shmem_pool serves the short-lived commands and replies of an
instance from one shmem and installs a larger one as the pool's shmem when an
allocation does not fit. The pool then holds that shmem, mapped and resident,
until later allocations have used up what is left of it. A reply of hundreds of
MiB, such as the data of vkGetPipelineCacheData for a large cache, therefore
left the pool holding a power-of-two shmem of up to twice the reply, on the
guest and on the host, long after the reply was consumed. The shmem cache would
not have kept a shmem that large, but the pool's own reference did.

Serve an allocation larger than 16 MiB from a shmem of its own that the pool
never holds: the caller owns the only reference, and the shmem is destroyed
when the caller drops it. Smaller allocations are suballocated as before. The
size policy is a plain header so that a test can cover it without a renderer.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
